<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">shaman</ansi>

The Shaman calls weather into a battle. Fog, a cold wind or rain settles over
the fight and changes both sides' odds for a few rounds; between calls the
Shaman answers with wind and lightning. It has no creed: no alignment gate
stands in front of any of its routes.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the Shaman is</ansi>

  Health      2 to start, 0.6 a level to level 20 (<ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
  Skill       Attack 0.7 and Evasion 0.8 a level (<ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>)
  Gear        light armor, no shield (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>)
  Mana        40, plus 10 a level (<ansi fg="command">help mana</ansi>)
  Stats       mysticism 4, vitality 2, perception 2, smarts 2 (<ansi fg="command">help growth</ansi>)
  Starter kit an ash staff, a hooded robe, a student's amulet, food, a
              waterskin, a knapsack and one minor mana draught
  Utility     Weather Sense, which forecasts the world's weather (<ansi fg="command">help forecast</ansi>)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The spells</ansi>

Stormcraft is the Shaman's school; only a Shaman may learn it.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Spell</ansi>        <ansi fg="yellow">level</ansi>  <ansi fg="yellow">mana</ansi>  <ansi fg="yellow">chant</ansi>  <ansi fg="yellow">what it does</ansi>
  Call Fog       1      6     1     for 3 rounds, foes' ranged attacks lose 10
                                    points of accuracy and their spells hit
                                    10% weaker (they are fogbound)
  Gust           1      5     2     a small wind spell, about 80% of Magic Missile
  Chill Wind     3      8     2     for 3 rounds, foes' spell chants and sling
                                    shots take one extra round to begin, as in
                                    the cold (they are windchilled)
  Rain           6     10     2     for 3 rounds, fire damage is halved on both
                                    sides and Lightning strikes 50% harder
  Lightning      8     12     2     a heavy bolt at one foe, 50% more in Rain

At level 5 the Shaman chooses its first talent, and at level 10 it promotes to
a Stormcaller, Mistweaver or Earthspeaker (<ansi fg="command">help shaman-routes</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How weather works</ansi>

A weather belongs to one battle. It never touches the world's weather
(<ansi fg="command">help weather</ansi>), which every player shares, and it ends with the battle.
Only one weather is up at a time: a new call replaces the old one, and the
foes' marks from the old one come off. A call lasts 3 rounds; a Mistweaver
and the Long Weather talent make it last longer. A foe that arrives after the
call is not marked by it. Weather never advances the world's clock.

The battle tells you when a weather is called, what it does, and when it
passes: <ansi fg="command">A gray fog rolls over the battle. (3 rounds, foe ranged attacks and
spells weaker)</ansi>, then <ansi fg="command">The fog thins and lifts.</ansi>. <ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi> shows the mark on a
foe you consider, and <ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi> lists Fogbound and Windchilled.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How a Shaman fights</ansi>

A battle plays out on its own. A Shaman's role is <ansi fg="command">caster</ansi>: with no weather up,
it calls one first. Chill Wind and Fog are worth their mana only against foes
that shoot or cast, so it saves them for those; it calls Rain once it knows
Lightning. Then it casts Lightning while mana lasts, else Gust, else swings.
<ansi fg="command">strategy me [role] [rule]</ansi> changes that (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>). Keep it in the back
row (<ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>) with a guardian in front (<ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>): a blow that
draws blood can break a chant (<ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Other Shamans</ansi>

A Shaman companion calls weather and casts the same way, knows the spells its
level allows, and promotes and chooses talents like any other
(<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>). Recruits are hired like any other and arrive with an ash staff.

Commands: <ansi fg="command">archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">class</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">talent</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">spells</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help shaman-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>.
